   "retrieve_ms": 925.8,
   "answer": "To zero the PX-200, first isolate the transmitter from the process and vent it to atmosphere for gauge models, or apply full vacuum for absolute models [1]. Then open the electronics housing cover and press and hold the ZERO button for five seconds, and the status LED will blink green three times when the new zero is accepted [1]. Alternatively, zeroing can be done remotely via HART using the \"Set PV Zero\" command [1]. Using a two- or three-valve manifold at installation makes it easier to isolate and zero the transmitter without removal [2]. Note that in liquid or steam service, zero should be verified annually, while clean, dry gas service does not require periodic recalibration [4].",
   "abstained": false,
