   "answer": "A slow upward drift in gas service usually points to condensate accumulating in the impulse line [1]. This is the most common cause of drift in gas service, and it's recommended to slope the impulse lines at least 1:12 and install a drain valve at the lowest point [2]. To fix this, drain the line and verify the slope per the installation guidance [1][2]. If the drift instead occurred after an overpressure event, it may indicate diaphragm damage—check for error code E-17 [1].",
