   "retrieve_ms": 218.4,
   "answer": "Two likely causes are documented for this symptom:\n\n1. **Fouled electrodes** – scale or grease deposits on the electrodes can reduce the measured signal, causing the meter to read zero or unusually low flow even while liquid is moving; remove the meter and clean the electrodes with a soft brush [1].\n2. **Empty pipe detection** – if error code E-17 appears, the pipe is not full at the sensor; ensure the pipe is completely full at the sensor location and check the installation position, since the meter must never be installed at the top of a pipe loop [6][7].\n\nYou should also verify grounding, since poor grounding is the most common cause of unstable readings, though this is more typically associated with erratic rather than zero readings [3].",
