   "context_recall": 1.0,
   "retrieve_ms": 210.2,
   "answer": "In ticket 1182, the PX-200 reading drift was traced to condensation in the impulse line [1]. This matches the manual's troubleshooting guidance, which states that a slowly upward-drifting reading in gas service usually indicates condensate accumulating in the impulse line [3]. The manual recommends draining the line, verifying the slope (at least 1:12) described in the installation section, and installing a drain valve at the lowest point of the impulse line [2][3].",
